+// REWINDBOX_RSX_LONG_IDLE_938: IPA 737 logs (COREPROF WAKE936, 14 Nov 2026). While the FIFO stays empty for seconds
+// the 50 us slices wake the RSX thread 16,600 times a second for nothing: Black Ops II frozen, 95 s, rsx_park=83,348
+// slices per 5 s window in one park period (park_ms 5,018); God of War III loading, 48,068 slices in 2.9 s. Once the
+// FIFO has been empty for long_idle_us without a break, the slice is long_slice_us. No game renders with its RSX idle
+// that long between two command bursts (it would show fewer than 4 images a second); a FIFO that idle is a loading
+// screen, a static or frozen screen or a pause. The first guest PUT after it is seen at most long_slice_us later (a
+// PUT is a plain store, never notified); a flush, flip or ZCULL request posted by another thread still wakes the
+// thread at once, as before. Frames, pacing and synchronisation are unchanged.
+constexpr std::uint64_t long_idle_us = 250'000;
+constexpr std::uint64_t long_slice_us = 1'000;
+
+constexpr std::uint64_t slice_for(std::uint64_t idle_us) noexcept
+{
+	return idle_us >= long_idle_us ? long_slice_us : slice_us;
+}
